description: >
  Enforces edit-in-place behavior, disables “card stacking,” and ensures
  that Cursor only modifies live integrated modules for the
  DKI Reporting Engine diagnostic system.

autoAttach:
  - "**/*.py"
  - "**/*.json"
  - "**/*.yml"
entryPoints:
  - "core.py"
  - "unified_diagnostic_system.py"
alwaysApply: true
---
# Cursor Repo Rules — Edit-in-Place, No Card Stacks

## Prime Directives
1) MODIFY EXISTING FILES IN-PLACE. Do not create new files, folders, or “examples” unless explicitly requested with a filename.
2) PRESERVE RUNTIME INTEGRATION. Every change must keep the project runnable from the documented entry points (`core.py`, `unified_diagnostic_system.py`, `__init__.py`).
3) RESPECT PACKAGE BOUNDARIES. Update imports and `__init__.py` when moving/renaming functions; ensure modules remain importable.
4) COHESION OVER FRAGMENTATION. Prefer refactors that integrate logic into the live modules over introducing helpers or stubs.
5) TEST LOCALLY. After edits, show the exact command to run (Windows/PowerShell examples first) and any required env vars.

## File Creation Rules
- DO NOT create new files by default.
- If a helper is truly necessary:
  - FIRST propose the exact file path and purpose in one sentence.
  - WAIT for explicit approval (a user message naming the file) before creating it.
- NEVER dump “sample scripts,” “snippets,” or “cards” outside the package.

## Refactor & Import Discipline
- When extracting a function/class, refactor in the SAME file unless user approves a new module.
- If a symbol moves, update all local imports and `__all__` in `__init__.py` accordingly.
- Keep public API stable; if breaking changes are unavoidable, list them succinctly.

## Execution Guarantees
- After edits, provide:
  - Run command (PowerShell): `python .\unified_diagnostic_system.py`
  - Alt entry (if any): `python .\core.py --mode run`
  - Env setup reminder if needed: `.venv\Scripts\activate` then `pip install -r requirements.txt`

## Style & Tooling
- Follow existing lint/format config if present. If not, use PEP8 and type hints, but DO NOT add new tooling files without permission.
- Log to the project’s configured logger; do not introduce ad-hoc prints except for temporary debug blocks labeled TODO:REMOVE.

## Forbidden Outputs
- No pseudo-files, no “card” examples, no duplicated shadow files, no notebooks, no placeholder “scaffolds,” unless explicitly requested.
- Do not rename top-level folders without explicit permission.

## Change Notes
- At the end of each change set, include a brief “What changed / Why / How to run” block.
